<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/kona-coast.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/kona-coast-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/kona-coast.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/island-communities/">Island communities</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Kailua-Kona</span></nav><p class="tag">Hawaii Island · West Hawaii</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser for Kailua-Kona Property Claims</h1><p class="lede">West Hawaii’s condos, coffee-country homes and coastal properties face vog, earthquakes and the occasional Kona storm. We help owners settle the amount of loss when the carrier’s number falls short.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn sun" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line-light" href="/contact-hawaii-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Hawaii County</dd></div><div><dt>Island</dt><dd>Hawaii Island</dd></div><div><dt>Service</dt><dd>On-site inspections</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="local"><div><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Kona storm wind and rain</li><li>Earthquake (usually separate coverage)</li><li>Vog and corrosion disputes</li><li>Condo water losses</li></ul></div><div><b class="h">Neighborhoods we cover</b><ul class="chips soft"><li>Kailua Village</li><li>Holualoa</li><li>Keauhou</li><li>Kalaoa</li><li>Kealakekua</li><li>Captain Cook</li><li>Kahaluu</li></ul></div><p><b>Housing:</b> Kona combines oceanfront and resort-area condominiums, subdivisions on the slopes of Hualalai, and older wood homes in coffee country upslope in Holualoa and South Kona.</p><p><b>History:</b> The 2006 Kiholo Bay earthquake damaged buildings in West Hawaii, the 2011 tsunami from Japan damaged some waterfront properties along the Kona coast, and vog from Kilauea often settles over the area.</p></div>
<h2>West Hawaii’s mix of property</h2>
<p>Kailua-Kona stretches from the oceanfront up the slopes of Hualalai. Along Alii Drive and around Kailua Village and Keauhou, condominiums and vacation rentals are common, many governed by AOAOs with master policies and sizeable deductibles. Subdivisions climb the hillside in Kalaoa and above town, while Holualoa and the coffee country of Kealakekua and Captain Cook hold older wood-frame homes, some on post-and-pier foundations and some relying on rain catchment. Kahaluu and the Keauhou area add resort-area and residential properties near the coast.</p>
<p>Because Kona is on the leeward side, it is drier and sunnier than Hilo, but that does not mean fewer claims. It means different ones.</p>
<h2>Event history on the Kona side</h2>
<p>The October 2006 Kiholo Bay earthquake shook West Hawaii, cracking walls and foundations and damaging some older buildings. In 2011, the tsunami generated off Japan reached the Kona coast and damaged some waterfront properties. Kona lows bring winter storms from the south and west – the reason they carry the Kona name – with heavy rain and wind hitting slopes that usually face calmer weather. Vog from Kilauea often drifts over the area, and its acidic particles are frequently cited when insurers argue that roof or metal damage is corrosion rather than a sudden loss.</p>
<h2>Common Kona disputes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Roof and metal flashing damage attributed to vog, salt air or UV rather than wind.</li>
<li>Condo water losses where the AOAO master policy and the owner’s HO-6 disagree on responsibility.</li>
<li>Earthquake-related cracking, which is often excluded unless separate earthquake coverage was purchased.</li>
<li>Short-term rental units where loss of rents or contents coverage is disputed.</li>
<li>Freight and labor costs in West Hawaii understated in carrier estimates.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Check for earthquake coverage</b>Standard homeowners policies generally exclude earth movement, including earthquake. If you have an earthquake endorsement or separate policy, its deductible and limits will shape any claim.</div>
<h2>How appraisal helps in West Hawaii</h2>
<p>If your insurer agrees a loss is covered but its estimate is too low, the appraisal clause may provide a path to a fair number without a lawsuit. Each side names an appraiser, and an umpire resolves anything they cannot agree on. Appraisal decides the amount of loss only. Coverage denials and questions about claim handling belong with a Hawaii attorney.</p>
<p>Hawaii Insurance Appraiser builds Kona estimates with local labor, freight and General Excise Tax, and documents the difference between long-term corrosion and storm damage. Learn about our <a href="/appraisal-specialties/kona-storm-high-wind-claims/">Kona storm and high-wind claims</a> work, our <a href="/appraisal-specialties/condo-aoao-commercial-appraisal/">condo and AOAO appraisal</a> service, or use the <a href="/island-claim-tools/claim-timeline-builder/">claim timeline builder</a> to organize your dates.</p>
<p>For condominium owners, the first step is often sorting out responsibility between the association and the unit owner. Once that is clear, the remaining question is usually price. Gather the association’s documents, both policies and the carrier’s estimate so the scope can be compared item by item against current West Hawaii costs.</p>
<h2>Specialties available in Kailua-Kona</h2><p>Every Hawaii Insurance Appraiser specialty is available to owners and associations in Kailua-Kona, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/appraisal-clause-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/homeowner-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/condo-aoao-commercial-appraisal/">Condo, AOAO &amp; Commercial</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/kona-storm-high-wind-claims/">Kona Storm &amp; High-Wind Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/hurricane-claim-appraisal/">Hurricane Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/fire-smoke-claim-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Claims</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Kailua-Kona owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can my insurer blame vog for damage to my Kona roof?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Insurers sometimes argue that vog or salt air caused gradual corrosion. If wind or another sudden event caused the damage, documentation and an independent inspection can help separate the two.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is earthquake damage to my Kailua-Kona home covered?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Usually not under a standard homeowners policy, which excludes earth movement. Coverage generally requires a separate earthquake policy or endorsement.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal work for a vacation rental condo in Keauhou?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>It can, if the loss is covered and the dispute is about the amount. Rental income and contents claims depend on the specific coverages in your policy.</p></div></details></div>
<h2>Nearby communities</h2><div class="related"><a href="/island-communities/hilo-big-island/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Hilo</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-communities/puna-pahoa-big-island/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Puna &amp; Pahoa</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="big" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn sun" href="/contact-hawaii-appraiser/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 7am–5pm HST</small></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Island communities</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/island-communities/honolulu-oahu/">Honolulu</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kailua-kaneohe-oahu/">Kailua &amp; Kaneohe</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/pearl-city-aiea-oahu/">Pearl City &amp; Aiea</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kapolei-ewa-beach-oahu/">Kapolei &amp; Ewa Beach</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/mililani-wahiawa-oahu/">Mililani &amp; Wahiawa</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/hilo-big-island/">Hilo</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kailua-kona-big-island/" aria-current="page">Kailua-Kona</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/puna-pahoa-big-island/">Puna &amp; Pahoa</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kahului-wailuku-maui/">Kahului &amp; Wailuku</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kihei-wailea-maui/">Kihei &amp; Wailea</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/lahaina-we